S5-07 strict N=2 residual ledger — 2026-11-17

Scope and actual comparator path
--------------------------------
This is an offline analysis of the counted common-ID source series
`s5-07-counted-canonical-n2-20261117-a`. Its strict within-series result is
`matches=false`. No guest replay, comparator edit, or allowlist edit was made
for this ledger.

The scalar/configuration/syscall checks pass, but the full
`stage4_nonce_variation_eligible` gate is false. It also requires the terminal
panic snapshot to pass `normalize_stage4_panic_snapshot`. Both source runs have
optional panic frames that the current allowlist rejects, so the panic
snapshot helper returns `None`; this disables both the machine stop volatility
projection and Stage4 UART normalization. The actual comparator therefore
compares the full nonce-normalized stop and UART bytes, after its explicit
removals of `com1_hex`, `com1_text`, and `machine_stop_reason` from the stop
object. The five-field volatility projection described in earlier analysis
was only a manual counterfactual and is not the strict comparator path.

